      "title": "Front matter",
      "pageStart": 1,
      "pageEnd": 8,
      "target": "../sections/sec-front-matter.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Two years of work that can transform the \nhealth system in a fragile setting  \nWHO’s response to COVID-19 in Somalia, 2020–2022:  \nroad to an inclusive recovery\nTwo years of work that can transform the \nhealth system in a fragile setting  \nWHO’s response to COVID-19 in Somalia, 2020–2022:\nroad to an inclusive recovery\nCopyright: © WHO Somalia, September 2022 \nPhotos © WHO Somalia/Fouzia Bano/Ismael Taxta/Arete\n© World Health Organization 2022\nSome rights reserved. This work is available under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 IGO licence (CC BY-NC-\nSA 3.0 IGO; https",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The front matter of the WHO report on its response to COVID-19 in Somalia, 2020–2022, published by the Eastern Mediterranean Regional Office, with copyright, licence, cataloguing data and ISBNs. The contents list six sections on crisis management, public health functions, vaccine roll-out, essential services, research and lessons for recovery. A foreword by the WHO Representative describes building testing, surveillance and treatment capacity in a fragile health system and names primary health care, essential public health functions and the health workforce as key areas for investment.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
